Local fix for SDL 3.4.14 (147a8ee32dbf9ac02f3794964490687b6bbda1bc, the
port's third_party/SDL), Nintendo 3DS audio driver (src/audio/n3ds), built
with devkitARM r68 and libctru 2.7.0. Independent of 0001.

N3DSAUDIO_CloseDevice skipped ndspChnReset(0) when the DSP had been
cancelled (DSPHOOK_ONCANCEL: the system cancelled the DSP's wake, APT's
WAKEUP_CANCEL or WAKEUP_CANCELALL). ndsp's channel 0 then still listed the
device's wave buffers, which live in device->hidden and are freed a few
lines later. That was harmless only while SDL held the last ndsp reference:
ndspExit then took ndsp down, and the next ndspInit cleared the list
(ndsp-channel.c, ndspiInitChn). When the program holds its own ndsp
reference as well, as the 3DS port does (3ds/i3DS.cpp), ndsp outlives the
device, and the next OpenDevice's ndspChnReset(0) walks the stale list:
it writes NDSP_WBUF_DONE into freed memory and follows its next pointers.
ndspChnReset only clears ndsp's CPU-side record of the channel under the
channel's lock and never waits for the DSP, so it is now done after a
cancel too.

Apply with: git -C <SDL clone> apply <this file> (tools/3ds/build_sdl.sh does)

diff --git a/src/audio/n3ds/SDL_n3dsaudio.c b/src/audio/n3ds/SDL_n3dsaudio.c
index ded98ea..c14865f 100644
--- a/src/audio/n3ds/SDL_n3dsaudio.c
+++ b/src/audio/n3ds/SDL_n3dsaudio.c
@@ -227,11 +227,14 @@ static void N3DSAUDIO_CloseDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
     dspUnhook(&dsp_hook);
     ndspSetCallback(NULL, NULL);
 
-    if (!device->hidden->isCancelled) {
-        ndspChnReset(0);
-        SDL_memset(device->hidden->waveBuf, 0, sizeof(ndspWaveBuf) * NUM_BUFFERS);
-        CondVar_Broadcast(&device->hidden->cv);
-    }
+    // Also after a cancel: ndspChnReset only clears ndsp's own record of the
+    // channel, under the channel's lock, and never waits for the DSP. Left
+    // out, the channel still lists the wave buffers in device->hidden, freed
+    // below; if ndsp outlives this device (something else holds it too), the
+    // next ndspChnReset(0), OpenDevice's, walks that list in freed memory.
+    ndspChnReset(0);
+    SDL_memset(device->hidden->waveBuf, 0, sizeof(ndspWaveBuf) * NUM_BUFFERS);
+    CondVar_Broadcast(&device->hidden->cv);
 
     contextUnlock(device);
 
